  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 138 AM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nUpper level high pressure that was centered over the High \nPlains region will begin to retrogrades west, leaving the High \nPlains in a northwest flow mid week to the end of the week. With\nthe region in northwest flow will see a series of disturbances \nmove through the area bringing daily chances for showers and \nthunderstorms Tuesday through Friday. At this time storm \ndevelopment will likely be isolated to scattered, as any \norganized convective setup is low. The ridge become more \namplified Friday with a stronger shortwave trof moving through \non Friday. As far as fire weather concerns in the long term, \nexpect fire weather conditions to remain low, despite the warm \ntemperatures, as increase low level moisture will keep min RH \nvalues at 30 percent or higher.",
